    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but small actions don't change the trajectory. it's all just a bandaid on a severed limb. i look at my friends or people i know and they're talking about buying houses or having kids in 10 years, and i just feel like i'm watching people decorate a sinking ship. it's hard to care about \"small actions\" when the math just doesn't add up. everything feels so heavy and empty.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
